    "overviewDetail": "The Cayman Islands is one of the worldΓÇÖs most established offshore financial centres, recognised for its tax-neutral environment, flexible corporate structures, and strong regulatory credibility. It is widely used by multinational corporations, investment funds, and high-net-worth individuals for international structuring and asset management.\n\nThe jurisdiction offers a streamlined incorporation process, typically allowing companies to be set up within a few days. The most common entity type is the exempted company, which is designed for businesses operating outside the local economy and allows 100% foreign ownership. There are no direct taxes imposed, including corporate income tax, capital gains tax, or withholding tax, making it highly attractive for cross-border operations.\n\nThe Cayman Islands Monetary Authority (CIMA) regulates financial services, ensuring compliance with global standards set by organisations such as the OECD and FATF. In recent years, the jurisdiction has strengthened its economic substance, anti-money laundering, and transparency frameworks to align with evolving international expectations.\n\nProviding a legal system based on English common law, a sophisticated financial services ecosystem, and continued regulatory evolution, the Cayman Islands remains a leading choice for global business structuring and investment vehicles.\n",
