        "id": 28,
        "question": "Why is the Cayman Islands considered tax-neutral?",
        "answer": "The jurisdiction does not impose corporate income tax, capital gains tax, or personal income tax, making it attractive for global structuring."
      },
      {
        "id": 29,
        "question": "What is an exempted company in the Cayman Islands?",
        "answer": "An exempted company is designed for businesses operating outside the local economy, commonly used for international investment and holding structures."
      },
      {
        "id": 30,
        "question": "Is the Cayman Islands compliant with global regulations?\n",
        "answer": "Yes, the jurisdiction aligns with OECD and FATF standards, including economic substance and transparency requirements."
